<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/2004">2004</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sheikh Zayed · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zayed bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a> was ruler of Abu Dhabi from 1966, when he replaced his brother Shakhbut, and used its new oil revenues for rapid development. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-saeed-al-maktoum">Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum</a> of Dubai he led the talks among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a> that created the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> in 1971, and he served as its first president until his death in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan" width="225" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Archives of the United Arab Emirates, Ministry of Presidential Affairs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheikh_Zayed_with_King_Faisal,_1974_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A month later <b>Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</b>, ruler of Abu Dhabi since 1966, and Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum of Dubai agreed at a meeting in the desert between their two emirates to form a union and invited the other rulers to join them.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1966 <b>Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</b> replaced his brother Shakhbut and used the revenues for development.</blockquote><a href="/state/sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi">Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi</a></li><li><blockquote>Rashid worked with <b>Zayed</b> of Abu Dhabi to form the United Arab Emirates, which Dubai joined at its foundation in December 1971.</blockquote><a href="/state/sheikhdom-of-dubai">Sheikhdom of Dubai</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Abu Dhabi, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">the United Arab Emirates</a>. Died in Abu Dhabi, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">the United Arab Emirates</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=24.45,54.4&amp;year=1973" aria-label="Abu Dhabi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5996 1263 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6446 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6446 1533h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=24.45,54.4&amp;year=1973">What was here in 1973? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
